{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>תִּתְעַלֵּם.</b> 'You must shut your eyes as though you did not see it.' (Rashi on Deut. 22:1, s.v. וְהִתְעַלַּמְתָּ)" "<b>תִּרְאֶה … תִּתְעַלֵּם.</b> 'You shall not see it' — that you should hide yourself from it; this is its plain sense. And our Rabbis said: there are times when you may hide yourself, etc. (Sifrei; Bava Metzia 30a)."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:47:55.217571676Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}